    description: "**Pass-21 finding (F3).** Distribution of `edge.meta.call_construct` across `edge.type='calls'` edges:\n\n```\ncall_construct = method      → 21,085 edges\ncall_construct = function    →    213 edges\ncall_construct = cross_file  →     78 edges\n```\n\n`method` and `function` are AST-construct kinds (what kind of call syntax). `cross_file` is a location descriptor (the call crosses a file boundary). They belong on different axes.\n\n**Cluster.** Third face of the INV-numat META pattern (vocabulary fields mix multiple semantic axes), alongside:\n- ADR-0031 (Symbol.language → discovery_language + protocol_origin)\n- ADR-0032 (Symbol.canonical_name → display_label + qualified_name)\n- WI-kadop (Symbol.origin → discovery_pass + synthesis_mechanism, filed 2026-06-01)\n\nBelongs as a sibling of WI-kadop under INV-numat.\n\n**Suggested fix.** Either:\n- Sub-divide `call_construct` value space by axis: keep `method` / `function` on the construct axis, and move `cross_file` to a new `call_locality` or `call_scope` field with values like `same_file` / `cross_file`.\n- Or rename `call_construct` to `call_kind` and add a new field for cross-file marker.\n\nADR-0024 style four-artifact axis declaration scaffolding (registry + dataclass field comment + ADR + validator entry) applies.\n\n**Lab notebook entry:** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_06012026_2310_pass21.md`."  # cb2c
    fields: {}  # cb2c
